Your Important Dates

These are all of the projected release dates that the Time Computation Unit has calculated for your sentence. These dates may change if you receive a disciplinary infraction and lose release credits, or if your release credits are restored. You may also see some dates appear or disappear depending on if you meet the qualifying criteria. Tap the button under any of the dates below to learn more about that release date and its criteria.

Standard Transition Program (STP)
5 days from today
December 21, 2021

Great work! Time Comp confirmed you've met the criteria for the Standard Transition Program. Make sure that your home plan is approved in order to walk out on this date. (Steer clear of disciplinary infractions, too — they can still put this date at risk.)

Learn more about STP
Community Supervision Begin Date (CSBD)
March 21, 2022Only eligible if criteria are met
(3 months and 5 days from today)

A discretionary release up to 90 days before your ERCD. You must meet the criteria listed in ADCRR Department Order 1002. You may also hear this called a “Temporary Release” (TR) date.

Learn more about CSBD
Earned Release Credit Date (ERCD)
June 6, 2022
(5 months and 21 days from today)

The earliest date you can be released based on Earned Release Credits.

Learn more about ERCD
Sentence Expiration Date (SED, “100%”, “Flat Time”)
September 16, 2022
(9 months from today)

The full term of your prison sentence (often called “100%” or “Flat Time”). You will be released on this date if you are not eligible for earlier release types. If you have to complete Community Supervision after your prison term, you must still agree to certain conditions of supervision.

Learn more about SED
Community Supervision End Date (CSED)
November 16, 2022
(11 months from today)

The last day that you can be under ADCRR supervision for your current sentence.

Learn more about CSED
